# Reference-rot detector, cron form (Linux / a jump box).
#
# On macOS prefer the launchd agents in this directory: modern macOS gates
# cron under TCC and ships no configured MTA, so MAILTO there silently
# discards every verdict — a check that runs and throws its answer away.
#
# Note both entries call the WRAPPERS, not rot-detector.sh directly. The
# wrapper bounds the run and leaves the receipt the heartbeat reads.
MAILTO=tiagobeltraoacioli@gmail.com

# Hourly: has anything rotted? Silent when clean (--quiet), so a quiet
# mailbox means a healthy fleet.
17 * * * * /opt/bloch/reference-integrity/detector-run.sh --quiet 2>&1

# Every 30 min: is the detector still running at all? A detector that stopped
# looks exactly like one that keeps passing — both are silence. Silent while
# the detector is fresh and clean; loud the moment it goes stale, starts
# failing, or was never loaded.
*/30 * * * * /opt/bloch/reference-integrity/heartbeat.sh --quiet 2>&1

# Daily: prove the DERIVATION still agrees with reality, which catches drift
# the peer check alone would miss (e.g. a unit added by hand with a
# hand-typed peer list).
23 6 * * * /opt/bloch/reference-integrity/derive-peers.sh check 2>&1
